{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/bundle_reader.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:03:16.457258Z","id":"294289dc10bfafc9bb11e6226dd1167aae6de34137c567b0d8e8519aa4726727","body":{"detail":"inflateAtMost caps output bytes but not work. archive 4.5.2's Inflate builds a full 2^maxCodeLength HuffmanTable (32,768 entries at code length 15) for every dynamic block (codecs/zlib/_huffman_table.dart), and a dynamic block that declares one 15-bit literal and an immediate end-of-block costs about 12 input bytes and yields nothing. Measured with flutter test on macOS: 100,000 such blocks (1.2 MB) took 2.6 s in inflateAtMost; a 2.4 MB manifest.json entry made of them took 5.6 s in BundleReader.read before it failed bad_manifest. A 32 MiB .clax (the §6.1 cap) is about 70 s, and manifest.json is inflated before step 3, so no key is needed. apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart:87 awaits BundleReader.read on the UI isolate, so the app freezes for that long. Spec §9 T3 answers memory, not work.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":156},"end":{"line":170},"content_hash":"8222a2cd976c03edbf285cf7a258b550d8c5e0e77921f3fa85b1ea4a412272e8"},"suggested_fix":"Bound the work per entry: refuse an entry whose compressed size exceeds its cap (256 KiB for manifest.json, the manifest size for files and seed; the writer only deflates when smaller), and count deflate blocks in inflateAtMost, refusing more than max/1024 + 16 of them. Run BundleReader.read in Isolate.run so even a legal 32 MiB bundle does not stall frames.","summary":"A crafted deflate stream costs about 2 s of CPU per MiB with no output, before the signature check","tags":["security","review:BF","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/signing.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:03:16.457924Z","id":"536fef68458dae52cc425a89ec3eb6dabd85f7b3f7c14ad9b9f993fc53f5e841","body":{"detail":"author.key = base64url of [1, 0 x 31] (the identity point) verifies the signature R = enc(aB), S = a mod L for every message, for any scalar a; a whole bundle with that key and a signature made without any private key reads through BundleReader.read. Under §6.5's first-use pin, every later bundle of that lineage under the same key is an update (with migrate.js), so anyone holding one copy can push updates to every install of it. Separately, cryptography 2.9.0's Ed25519Point.equals (lib/src/dart/ed25519_impl.dart:53-80) compares X twice and never Y, so verify accepts sB equal to the point (x, -y) of R + hA: with the identity key, R' = (x, -y) of aB and S = a mod L also verifies. Canonical S and y < p are checked, so the doc comment's 'strict' holds for encodings only. No forgery under an honest prime-order key follows from either, but the 'verified strictly' of spec §4.5 is not what this checks.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":66},"end":{"line":88},"content_hash":"4060e12405c89ee248526d70ff5542f91a4cf63cbf5364169d9af12fb5bcca60"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse author.key and the signature's R when they are one of the small-order encodings (the 8 torsion points; libsodium's blocklist), and compare the encoded points rather than relying on Ed25519Point.equals, or use a verifier with strict semantics. Add a test with the identity key.","summary":"verifyManifest accepts a small-order author.key, under which anyone can sign any manifest; the library's point comparison checks only X","tags":["security","review:BF","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/manifest.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:03:16.457980Z","id":"032ebf00940c8741ee25aef909762cf175080f7d3adba00d8a040c44c0c374b1","body":{"detail":"Manifest.parse and _seedDocs (bundle_reader.dart:348-388) accept any JSON depth: capabilities {\"x\": 100,000 nested arrays} (200 KB, under the 256 KiB manifest cap) parses, signs and reads, and jsonEncode of the parsed value then throws StackOverflowError. The installer passes capabilities to the daemon unchanged and sends seed documents as JSON, so the failure lands there as an Error rather than a BundleError, after the person has seen the install sheet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":313},"end":{"line":323},"content_hash":"cb7dc15e7a11670139c5bdafbccd1997b3353077ce84fa52bc879a952e88dea4"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse capabilities and each seed line's data deeper than a fixed cap (64 is ample) with bad_manifest / bad_seed, and test it.","summary":"capabilities and seed data have no nesting depth cap; re-encoding a deep value throws StackOverflowError","tags":["review:BF","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/bundle_reader.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:03:16.458032Z","id":"4f56b9edfb640f68b0978b38569362812e3d46c8e7d4847a5707b3f581a8a0ee","body":{"detail":"_entries checks that cdOffset + cdSize equals the end record's offset, but not that the first local header is at 0, that each entry's data ends where the next local header starts, or that the central walk ends at cdOffset + cdSize. A valid bundle with 4 KiB of junk prepended (offsets shifted) reads, so a polyglot file passes, and Bundle.bytes, kept byte for byte for re-share, carries the junk. §4.1 says no other entry is allowed; the writer emits none of this.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":280},"end":{"line":342},"content_hash":"e0c8672ff7c2bd657bd0fb636796ba4e0d345daa40dc2e3f9aefaf169bbc76e6"},"suggested_fix":"Require local headers to be contiguous from offset 0 in central order and the central walk to end exactly at the end record.","summary":"Bytes before the first entry, between entries and after the last central entry are accepted","tags":["review:BF","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/manifest.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:03:16.458081Z","id":"754ef8db79e7f4cb89a3bbd594ca3df491a47caf535b87dbfa94cd0d1f03b8cf","body":{"detail":"A manifest with title 'Bank\\u202Egnp.exe\\n\\u0000' and author.name 'Alex\\u200B\\u0007' reads. §9 T10 rests on the sheets showing the name as the sender's claim beside the fingerprint; a right-to-left override, zero-width or newline makes that claim render as something else.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":365},"end":{"line":369},"content_hash":"bf44f67f526b699f28dbd9a8deb813828e974852af18d2db67850a5fad36bc47"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse C0/C1 controls, U+200B-U+200F, U+202A-U+202E and U+2066-U+2069 in title and author.name with bad_manifest.","summary":"title and author.name accept control and bidi-override characters","tags":["review:BF","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/lineage_store.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:56:44.443350Z","id":"087058cc74ccdac30aa4d1a62cdb87868f22b1c7ec20613ed2657f115b7fb4a4","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md §5.3 says an artifact_deleted event for <aid> removes its lineage entry and kept bundle, and §6.5 relies on it (deleting the app forgets the pin). The store offers forget(aid); the subscription to the daemon's events lives with the services or lib/app.dart, which must call it. Until then a deleted installed app's entry keeps matching its lineage in decide (lib/bundle/trust.dart), and a re-received bundle shows update/older/current against an app that no longer exists.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":277},"end":{"line":284},"content_hash":"7097996b39736523795bed06ecf7cf492eff2b00bf0f23b15429ea069dfb98c5"},"summary":"Nothing calls LineageStore.forget on artifact_deleted yet","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/lineage_store.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:00:41.911194Z","id":"ab843a72851f426c7e74f379fea05164a19924d7e5bfd5e09d1175dd80a8dcda","body":{"detail":"_readRaw returns {} on FormatException or a non-object root, and put/forget/stopUpdates then write that map back over the file. One unparseable file (disk fault, a later format change read by an older build) silently loses every author lineage (the next export mints a new lineage, so recipients get a separate app instead of an update), every installed app's key pin and its released list, and leaves the kept bundles under bundles/ orphaned. It is safe for trust (a lost pin yields install as a new app, never an update of an existing one) but unrecoverable. The test at test/bundle/lineage_store_test.dart:34 covers the empty read, not the write that follows.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":303},"end":{"line":312},"content_hash":"450580fd998ab40d66bbc542c6858f9fb12ffd5f87f3b7ead8983a9a23c09148"},"suggested_fix":"On a parse failure, move the file aside (lineages.json.bad-<time>) before the first write, or refuse writes until it is dealt with; test put after a malformed file.","summary":"A malformed lineages.json reads as empty and the next write erases every lineage","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/lineage_store.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:00:41.911229Z","id":"906f5ee561054885cb6c24e891dbe97e031ce6581559f198d15a258a4bbe2446","body":{"detail":"Callers read an entry, await other work, then put a derived entry: stopUpdates awaits entry() before put, and the updater (§8.2) will hold an entry across daemon calls before writing withRelease. A forget(aid) from artifact_deleted (087058cc) or another write landing in that gap is undone: the deleted app's entry and pin come back and keep matching its lineage in decide.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":263},"end":{"line":275},"content_hash":"ce5e73320f4a45e2b64a7d42d07acb3b4e3c6a2c121d7d97fd7fc7ca90a97922"},"suggested_fix":"Offer update(aid, LineageEntry Function(LineageEntry) change) that reads and writes in one synchronous step and does nothing when the entry is gone; use it in stopUpdates.","summary":"put is a blind overwrite, so a stale entry written after forget resurrects a deleted app","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/trust.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:56:44.443540Z","id":"01dfd17f5af82d8954ea7e6ce56073e1c49306d39c3f9f11ae8686fa265ff4fa","body":{"detail":"§6.4 of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md asks update to carry modified from §5.4, which needs the live version's content_sha256 and capabilities; the lineage store does not hold them. decide therefore takes an optional named live: {aid: ReleaseState}. The caller fetches the live state of local apps whose entry has the bundle's lineage (GET /api/artifacts/<aid>) and passes it; an app missing from live counts as modified, so the sheet offers 'Update (replaces your changes)' rather than silently replacing changes.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":56},"end":{"line":112},"content_hash":"405021f6c18de569a9ca2ab9953c6cae2d2fcf759d16f1038a65abc33e7b7752"},"summary":"decide takes a live map beyond the spec's decide(bundle, store, ownKey)","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/trust.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:00:41.911066Z","id":"47edb0d61239aff86bcd7fe7e7607c233e7ff3fa7eef7463c93cf5aa45ac04f7","body":{"detail":"decide answers own only when ownKey is non-null and equals author.key. When the caller cannot read the seed (macOS keychain prompt denied, BundleKey.existing throwing on a bad seed) and passes null, the person's own re-received bundle skips own, matches no installed entry, and lands on foreign at lines 137-139 against their own author entry: 'already installed from someone else', Install separately. ownKey adds nothing here: an author entry with the bundle's lineage and key exists only because this install signed with that key, so matching role author + lineage + key alone answers own without touching the keychain on every import (each read of a second keychain item is one more prompt per process on ad-hoc macOS builds). Also unhandled: an own-key bundle whose lineage has no local author entry (the author deleted the app) answers install and creates a role installed entry under the person's own key, so their next modified export forks instead of continuing the lineage. test/bundle/trust_test.dart has no case for ownKey null with an author entry, nor own key with no author entry.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":82},"end":{"line":91},"content_hash":"3544ad15409787fc5ab990fe63164dc198271891a140e5bf0531d67ef9b47133"},"suggested_fix":"Match own on (role author, lineage, key) without ownKey, drop the keychain read from the import path, and add the two tests.","summary":"own needs ownKey from the keychain; without it the person's own app reads as foreign","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/trust.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:00:41.911152Z","id":"c9545e1b03adf56958e6f0e8b56422c5c3dd741096769b93de7fa830b2299c02","body":{"detail":"§6.4 of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md defines forked as 'a local fork has the lineage and key as upstream'. Today only a fork sets upstream (§8.1 step 4 writes installed entries without it), so the result is right. If an installer ever copies a received bundle's forked_from into upstream, any bundle claiming forked_from of a lineage it does not own would make later genuine bundles of that lineage show 'You made <title> your own'.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":131},"end":{"line":135},"content_hash":"de87e4fd0f435fcf4a98685289879895881d0e9e0eca0ffbf30a202dca274390"},"suggested_fix":"Add e.role == LineageRole.author to the test and a case with an installed entry carrying upstream.","summary":"forked matches any entry with a matching upstream, not only a local fork (role author)","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/trust.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:00:41.911364Z","id":"84e3adb08a80639c839903ba1b91e3a3c5db8b1bcc60779e59468db21e1ad8a9","body":{"detail":"With live omitted every update carries modified: true, so the sheet offers 'Update (replaces your changes)' / 'Keep mine' and nothing is replaced silently; current, conflict and older do not depend on it. The cost of a caller forgetting it is an unneeded question, and a 'Keep mine' answer that stops updates for an app that had no changes. An aid missing from live because the app was deleted (087058cc) also counts as modified and is offered an update; a caller that gets a 404 for the live state should forget the entry and decide again.","kind":"comment","references":"01dfd17f5af82d8954ea7e6ce56073e1c49306d39c3f9f11ae8686fa265ff4fa","span":{"start":{"line":56},"end":{"line":112},"content_hash":"405021f6c18de569a9ca2ab9953c6cae2d2fcf759d16f1038a65abc33e7b7752"},"summary":"Reviewed: the live parameter is sound and safe by default","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/trust.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:03:52.166741Z","id":"c0992728a69e7d4f271305cea58dc276c640597e08ae31e632265c6b3f9bada5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:12ebb6b8","summary":"decide answers own on an author entry with the bundle's lineage and key, without ownKey; TrustDecision.mine marks a bundle signed by this install's key, so on install (own app deleted here) the installer can record role author. Evidence: flutter test test/bundle/trust_test.dart test/bundle/lineage_store_test.dart test/platform/bundle_key_test.dart -> +36, All tests passed, including 'own without the keychain: an author entry with the lineage and key' and 'own bundle after deleting the app: install, marked as mine'.","supersedes":"47edb0d61239aff86bcd7fe7e7607c233e7ff3fa7eef7463c93cf5aa45ac04f7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/trust.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:03:52.168166Z","id":"bb7bd1db031b9a38a92283cd435e3ed0951ae4725ff947a7e180527e9c75e190","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:12ebb6b8","summary":"forked now requires a local entry with role author. Evidence: flutter test test/bundle/trust_test.dart test/bundle/lineage_store_test.dart test/platform/bundle_key_test.dart -> +36, All tests passed, including the installed-entry-with-upstream case in 'forked: a local fork names the lineage and key upstream'.","supersedes":"c9545e1b03adf56958e6f0e8b56422c5c3dd741096769b93de7fa830b2299c02","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/lineage_store.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:03:52.169362Z","id":"031ea4f72fd0d01bdc936ecc43a7c0b5a0dfd09ba4f4708bd6d89cac397b7eaf","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:12ebb6b8","summary":"A damaged lineages.json reads as empty and sets LineageStore.damaged; the next mutation renames it to lineages.json.corrupt-<ms> (LineageStore.setAside) before writing, and a file that exists but cannot be read throws rather than being overwritten. Evidence: flutter test test/bundle/trust_test.dart test/bundle/lineage_store_test.dart test/platform/bundle_key_test.dart -> +36, All tests passed, including 'a malformed file is set aside before a write, and reported'.","supersedes":"ab843a72851f426c7e74f379fea05164a19924d7e5bfd5e09d1175dd80a8dcda","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/lineage_store.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:03:52.170550Z","id":"7c926e937bbe952462303b47577bebbeeb5f636f030f33f55f72d78fa73e1f36","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:12ebb6b8","summary":"Mutations run under one lock; update(aid, change) re-reads under it; an artifact ID forgotten in this process drops later put/update/keepBundle. Evidence: flutter test test/bundle/trust_test.dart test/bundle/lineage_store_test.dart test/platform/bundle_key_test.dart -> +36, All tests passed, including 'a forget during an update stays forgotten' (also a stale put after forget).","supersedes":"906f5ee561054885cb6c24e891dbe97e031ce6581559f198d15a258a4bbe2446","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/lineage_store.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:10:03.474157Z","id":"950816c0523a4a99812e9fe3ada001f21e10d4deed89871a74c3b07e43b162bf","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"087058cc74ccdac30aa4d1a62cdb87868f22b1c7ec20613ed2657f115b7fb4a4","summary":"forgetDeleted(events, store, snapshots:) in apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart subscribes and calls forget (commit 8b0309e2); Installer.open also forgets an entry whose app the daemon answers 404 for. Open until apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart subscribes it.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:10:03.474210Z","id":"a68839b90d671e20e615a886ae8e473aff8ce2f90fdfa7f3b3c811e0c959fc89","body":{"detail":"Section 8.4 of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md restores a snapshot left by an update interrupted during its live migrate.js run, at the next start. recoverInterrupted does it and returns the notices to show once; apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart must call it after the daemon is up. Until then an interrupted update leaves the app on the new version with partly migrated documents and the snapshot file in <support>/snapshots/.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":335},"end":{"line":336},"content_hash":"01eaa0ad5e9be1a0acfc700fdbd66d856a68b1c489c59a9fe45abc92deff85f5"},"summary":"Nothing calls Updater.recoverInterrupted at the app's start yet","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:10:03.474246Z","id":"874d8a675377fe7ba911cf8c9c558a1ac81427968e8956d90211dd52e2484871","body":{"detail":"update takes no cancelled future; each step relies on the inspector's limits (runMigration total, runTests total, inspect settle). The progress sheet therefore has no Cancel. Acceptable while the sheet is modal and the limits are tens of seconds.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":175},"end":{"line":176},"content_hash":"644b1a97a095e0d483b799cfa64b50297ebd45570f22864ad2d102586e1b7b3d"},"summary":"An update cannot be cancelled, and a hung inspector holds it for the inspector's own limits","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/bundle_reader.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:10:33.912198Z","id":"ce8aee0e07cde51cdf439719d1c67698ad6c62cf24b0b9228ff85a966a59d721","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:82aaa7aa","summary":"inflateAtMost caps deflate blocks at 2 + max/8192 and _Entry.inflate refuses a compressed size over max + 1 KiB; BundleReader.read runs files over 16 KiB on Isolate.run. The 20,000-empty-dynamic-block stream (1,061 ms uncapped) is refused: format_reader_test.dart \"many empty dynamic blocks are refused, not inflated\" (manifest.json: too_large) and \"a file over the inline size reads on another isolate\" pass. Residual: all files may declare 64 MiB in all, about 8,200 blocks or roughly 0.4 s, on the background isolate.","supersedes":"294289dc10bfafc9bb11e6226dd1167aae6de34137c567b0d8e8519aa4726727","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/bundle_reader.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:10:33.913664Z","id":"44d3cad12924e70b18d694dc0c58b7335d54a65872da4491fe19440abeb204c4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:82aaa7aa","summary":"_entries requires local headers end to end from offset 0 in central order with no local extra field, the last entry to end at the central directory, and the central walk to end at the end record. format_reader_test.dart group \"bytes outside the entries\" (before, between, after the last entry, after the end record) passes.","supersedes":"4f56b9edfb640f68b0978b38569362812e3d46c8e7d4847a5707b3f581a8a0ee","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/manifest.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:10:33.914932Z","id":"1213d1d48893b0d72c1530bd98527ceb28ac4e8220e01c7a90c3c96b540d9cee","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:82aaa7aa","summary":"withinJsonDepth (manifest.dart) caps capabilities and seed data at 64 levels: bad_manifest and bad_seed. format_reader_test.dart group \"JSON depth\" passes, including a 100,000-deep seed value refused without a StackOverflowError.","supersedes":"032ebf00940c8741ee25aef909762cf175080f7d3adba00d8a040c44c0c374b1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/manifest.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:10:33.916161Z","id":"a503c6c5b675bee570243c1634af10a5bbc05e7d5596c7fcaf7b368031c5cc5f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:82aaa7aa","summary":"Manifest refuses title and author.name holding C0/C1 controls, U+061C, U+200B, U+200E/F, U+2028-202E, U+2060, U+2066-2069, U+FEFF (bad_manifest); ZWJ and ZWNJ stay allowed. format_manifest_test.dart \"title and author name refuse hidden and direction characters\" passes.","supersedes":"754ef8db79e7f4cb89a3bbd594ca3df491a47caf535b87dbfa94cd0d1f03b8cf","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/signing.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:10:33.917357Z","id":"bcac00150fbbac916b5cd7dfa52104747f6388e6e46dabc0b9ec789f7c4808e2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:82aaa7aa","summary":"verifyStrict (apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/signing.dart) refuses a key with [8]A = identity and compares the re-encoded [S]B - [h]A with R byte for byte, no longer using cryptography Ed25519Point.equals. test/bundle/format_hash_signing_test.dart: \"a small-order author key is refused\" (identity and y=-1 keys), \"R is compared by its bytes, so (x, -y) of R fails\", \"RFC 8032 tests 1 to 3 sign and verify\", \"a BundleKey identity signs bundles that verify\" pass; flutter test test/bundle/: +126, all passed.","supersedes":"536fef68458dae52cc425a89ec3eb6dabd85f7b3f7c14ad9b9f993fc53f5e841","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/lineage_store.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:14:16.124660Z","id":"7f35976013de1cec8f23ecb74fb7c3f14afd4e993ae19ce3d5e43922886ec025","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:46990f7c","summary":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart _startBundles subscribes forgetDeleted(api.events(types: ['artifact_deleted']), _lineages, snapshots:) once the daemon is first up. Evidence: flutter test test/app_bundles_test.dart, 'a deleted app’s lineage is forgotten' passes (+3: All tests passed).","supersedes":"087058cc74ccdac30aa4d1a62cdb87868f22b1c7ec20613ed2657f115b7fb4a4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/signing.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:14:48.411972Z","id":"41ecf850e35b8d12e5960a1f58697a5e8c8542f25f5992df944d6c8b18c8d109","body":{"detail":"Since d0abcbc9, verifyStrict in apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/signing.dart refuses an author.key on libsodium's has_small_order blocklist (smallOrderEncodings: the seven encodings, sign bit ignored) and an S not below L (a byte comparison), then calls cryptography 2.9.0's DartEd25519.verify. The BigInt verifier of 82aaa7aa is removed. Tests in test/bundle/format_hash_signing_test.dart: RFC 8032 tests 1-3, the identity-key forgery passes the library alone but is refused, every blocklisted encoding refused with either sign bit, tampered signatures fail, a BundleKey identity verifies. The library's Ed25519Point.equals (X only) remains in the path: it also accepts [S]B = (x, -y) of R + [h]A. That point is -(R + [h]A) + T with T = (0, -1) of order 2, so with a key outside the blocklist an acceptance needs [-S]B = R0 + [h]A for R = R0 + T and h = H(R, A, M), the same equation as an ordinary forgery under A: not exploitable without the private key. It does make verification non-strict (a signature can be accepted that RFC 8032's cofactorless check rejects), so a second verifier may disagree on crafted signatures; no test, since showing it needs the point arithmetic this decision removes.","kind":"comment","references":"bcac00150fbbac916b5cd7dfa52104747f6388e6e46dabc0b9ec789f7c4808e2","summary":"Owner decision 2026-10-14: verify with an off-the-shelf implementation, no hand-written curve arithmetic","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
